{"message":"You’re correct that reporting after the 2-business-day window but within 60 days can mean liability of up to $500. Since this transaction is $412.88, your potential liability for this charge would be no more than $412.88—not more than the transaction amount.

I’m unable to file the TechWorld dispute right now because your Light Blue checking account already has its maximum two open debit-card disputes: the existing $189.99 dispute and the $275.00 EveryonePay fraud dispute. Your account is also protected with the replacement card order already placed.

Would you like me to transfer you to a human agent to review this additional fraud claim and the open-dispute limit?"}
